{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "ff0e1abc-733f-59ff-9af5-3e0382474bd6"/*LoadVdbExample*/,
  "Description": "[LoadVdb] reads OpenVDB files as written by Houdini, Blender or TiXL itself. The bunny is a level set: made coarser with [VolumeResample], meshed and scaled down. The plume is a fog volume: [VolumeToNanoVdb] uploads it and [VdbDensityField] makes its density a field for [RaymarchField]. [VolumeInfo] reports what a file contains.\n\nAKA: vdb, openvdb, houdini, import, file, bunny, smoke, cloud\n\nTips\n- Smaller VoxelSize means sharper surfaces and more memory and time; start coarse and refine.\n- Level sets store signed distance in world units (negative inside); fog volumes store density.\n- Files are watched and reload when they change on disk.\n- A file with several grids: pick one with GridName.",
